+/*
+ * Vendor page backdrop (patch 0242) -- one scene per vendor
+ * (Blacksmith/Alchemist/Enchanter), the same room each vendor's own
+ * dedicated crafting/enhance/scrap stations already show in their own
+ * modals (.craft-scene etc. below), now behind the vendor's whole page
+ * too. Deliberately NOT the locked-aspect-ratio .craft-scene treatment --
+ * that shape exists for pixel-perfect hit-targets landing on painted
+ * frames, and this page has none: its height varies with content (a
+ * short upgrade list vs. a big stock grid), so a locked ratio + 100%/100%
+ * stretch would distort the art the moment content height doesn't match
+ * the image's own ratio. Plain cover/center instead, same reasoning
+ * .fund-guild-scene above already uses for its own no-hit-target
+ * backdrop -- and the same translucent dark backing .fund-guild-content
+ * uses over its own art, so cards/text on top stay legible regardless of
+ * how bright a given vendor's room art is.
+ *
+ * `min-height: 100%` is load-bearing, not decorative -- without it this
+ * div sizes to its own content only (the header card + upgrade grid +
+ * stock list), which on a short page (few upgrades, small stock grid)
+ * left a visible seam where the art just stopped partway down and the
+ * plain panel backdrop showed through underneath -- the background
+ * looked like it was painted onto the vendor-card specifically rather
+ * than the page. `.panel` (this div's actual container -- VendorPage's
+ * Fragment contributes no DOM node of its own, so .vendor-scene is a
+ * direct child) gets a definite height from `.menu-body`'s `flex: 1`,
+ * which is exactly why a plain `100%` here resolves correctly instead of
+ * collapsing to 0 the way percentage heights usually do without a
+ * definite ancestor. `min-` rather than a flat `height` so a genuinely
+ * tall page (a big Stock grid) still grows the scene to match rather
+ * than clipping it.
+ */
+.vendor-scene {
+  position: relative;
+  min-height: 100%;
+  border-radius: 8px;
+  overflow: hidden;
+  background-size: cover;
+  background-position: top center;
+  background-color: var(--night);
+}
+.vendor-scene-content {
+  position: relative;
+  padding: 14px;
+  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--night) 45%, transparent);
+}
+
 .locked-upgrade {
   opacity: 0.5;
   border-style: dashed;
@@ -2877,6 +2923,24 @@ button.harvest-item:hover {
   overflow: hidden;
 }
 
